<title>HONG KONG: Japan hit by earthquake - Hong Kong observatory.</title>
<headline>Japan hit by earthquake - Hong Kong observatory.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>A strong earthquake estimated at 5.3 on the open-ended Richter scale was detected on the main Japanese island of Honshu on Saturday, Hong Kong's Royal Observatory said.</p>
<p>The epicentre of the quake, detected at 1:56 a.m. Hong Kong time (1756 GMT), was initially located at about 90 km (55.9 miles) east of the city of Nagoya.</p>
<p>The observatory gave no further details.</p>
</text>
